// Pull request author: clivoa
// Change: new rule
// Title: Sensitive Data Archived Via Ditto - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 7b1f4c62-9e83-4a51-bb27-6d0c3e5a8f14
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: clivoa
// Date: 2026-08-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: collection, T1560.001, T1005
// Description: Detects the "ditto" utility archiving a path that holds credentials, browser secrets or
//   cryptocurrency wallet data. "ditto" is Apple's own copy and archive tool and preserves resource
//   forks and extended attributes, which is why macOS infostealers use it to stage collected data
//   into a single archive before exfiltration. AMOS collects Keychain files, browser credentials and
//   wallet data and compresses them with "ditto" into an archive in "/tmp" prior to upload.
// False positives:
//   - Backup or migration tooling that archives the Keychain directory or SSH keys on a schedule
//   - A user archiving their own SSH keys or browser profile before moving to another machine
// References:
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/ditto/
//   - https://www.cyberproof.com/blog/inside-amos-stealer-how-this-threat-targets-macos-credentials-and-keychains/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9f2bb9f58dd827f437af4825c9ed12df44fd1281/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_sensitive_data_archived_via_ditto.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/ditto" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/Library/Keychains" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/.ssh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Login Data" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Cookies" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Extension Settings" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Exodus" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Electrum" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/Ledger Live")
